        body: "**HERNIA AND PTLD**\n\u2022 Incisional hernia can present with severe pain and bowel obstruction when abdominal contents become incarcerated and/or strangulated; it can also present as an asymptomatic bulge or with vague abdominal pain and/or fullness. [4]\n\u2022 PTLD presentation is often nonspecific, with no or vague symptoms such as fevers, night sweats or weight loss; imaging may show bulky lymphadenopathy, and biopsy confirms the diagnosis. [4]\n\n**KIDNEY**\n\u2022 Proteinuria may be absent even with advanced kidney disease because of the antiproteinuric effect of calcineurin inhibitors. [4]\n\u2022 Table 4 lists nephrotoxicity, electrolyte disorders, neurotoxicity and hypertension among calcineurin inhibitor side effects. [3]\n\u2022 Not in the guideline: symptoms, levels or management for neurotoxicity, hyperkalemia or magnesium disorders. [3]\n\n**STEROIDS**\n\u2022 Not in the guideline: stress-dose steroid or adrenal insufficiency advice. [3]\n\u2022 Corticosteroids are among the maintenance agents (Table 4). [3]\n\n**MORE**\nRelated consults: [Potassium](#/tree/potassium) (high potassium); [Adrenal insufficiency](#/tree/adrenal-insufficiency) (steroid use); [Abdominal pain hub](#/tree/abdominal-pain-hub) (abdominal pain).\nDetail: [late-problems detail](#/info/tpe-liver-chronic-detail).",
