        summary: 'Lung recipients, possible alloimmune ALAD (ISHLT): pulse steroids, IVIg, lymphocyte-depleting agents or plasma exchange may be considered (reached consensus), no doses (call the transplant team first).',
        body: [
            'For possible alloimmune ALAD, pulse steroids, IVIg, lymphocyte-depleting agents or plasma exchange may be considered (reached consensus), chosen by local availability, severity and patient factors (call the transplant team first). Bronchoscopy with BAL and biopsy seeks at least five evaluable fragments. [5]',
            '',
            '**AMR with allograft dysfunction** should always be treated with multiple drugs or interventions (reached consensus). [6]',
            '',
            'Patients on augmented immunosuppression should be monitored closely for secondary opportunistic infections (reached consensus). [5]',
            '',
            '**Antifungal prophylaxis:** IDSA 2016 recommends restarting it in lung recipients given augmented immunosuppression with thymoglobulin, alemtuzumab or high-dose corticosteroids (IDSA grade: strong recommendation, moderate-quality evidence). IDSA 2026 makes no recommendation for or against universal or targeted prophylaxis (IDSA: knowledge gap) and does not say the 2016 statement is withdrawn. [8][9]',
            '',
            'Retransplantation could be considered for selected patients with severe ALAD (reached consensus; votes widely spread), with considerable caution. [5]',
            '',
            'Not in the documents: doses for any rejection treatment, or a specific AMR regimen. Nearest fact: there have been no randomized-controlled trials, systematic reviews, or head-to-head comparisons of different AMR treatments. [6]',
            '',
            'Related consults: [ECMO](#/tree/ecmo) (candidacy), [Sepsis](#/tree/sepsis) (infection bundle); [detail](#/info/tpe-lung-specialist-care).',
        ].join('\n'),
