        summary: "CMV consensus 2025: recommended: IV ganciclovir in severe or life-threatening disease; oral valganciclovir in mild to moderate disease if the patient can tolerate and adhere (strong, moderate).",
        body: "**FIRST-LINE, normal kidney function (strong, moderate):** [Valganciclovir](#/drug/valganciclovir/cmv-treatment) 900 mg every 12 h, or [Ganciclovir](#/drug/ganciclovir/cmv-treatment) 5 mg/kg IV every 12 h. Below normal kidney function: [kidney dose bands](#/info/tpe-cmv-dosing).\n\u2022 IV ganciclovir is recommended in life-threatening and severe disease (strong, low); preferred for life- or sight-threatening disease when optimal drug exposure is essential. [22]\n\u2022 Oral valganciclovir is recommended in mild to moderate disease if oral therapy is tolerated and adhered to (strong, moderate). [22]\n\u2022 Liver guideline (liver recipients): IV ganciclovir if viral load is 100,000 IU/mL or more, absorption is impaired or infection is severe (Strong, Level 1); the sources differ. [23]\n\u2022 Valcyte label: transplant indication is prevention; this page's treatment doses rest on the guideline ([Guideline and label differ](#/info/tpe-cmv-dosing)). [24]\n\nEditor note: the guideline does not say whether to start an antiviral in the ED before a result is back; agree this with the transplant team before the first dose.\n\nDuring treatment, weekly CMV DNA is recommended (strong, high). [22]\n\nRelated consults: [Sepsis](#/tree/sepsis) fever, shock; [Pneumonia](#/tree/pneumonia) lung disease; [Diarrhea](#/tree/diarrhea) gut disease.",
