        type: "info",
        module: 4,
        title: "Fever with low neutrophils in a transplant recipient",
        safetyLevel: "warning",
        summary: "Fever with low neutrophils: Sepsis consult's empiric antibiotics without delay (editor note). Review (emergency medicine, 2018): time-sensitive emergency. Not in the labels or guidelines used: a transplant-specific regimen.",
        body: "\nEditor note: give the Sepsis consult's empiric antibiotics without delay; the febrile neutropenia pathway's risk score is written for cancer patients; call the transplant team.\n\u2022 Review (emergency medicine, 2018; solid organ and stem cell transplant patients; a narrative review, not a guideline): sepsis and neutropenic fever are life-threatening emergencies; both are time-sensitive diagnoses. [40]\n\u2022 Not in the labels or guidelines used: a transplant-specific regimen, or how the cancer febrile-neutropenia pathway, including its risk score, applies to a transplant recipient with drug-induced neutropenia.\n\u2022 KDIGO 2009, non-transplant population: with drug-induced neutropenia (ANC below 500/\u00b5L), patients are at increased risk for serious infection (ungraded). [57]\n\u2022 App content: the febrile neutropenia pathway's risk score and references are written for cancer patients, and its low-risk branch requires an oncologist's agreement.\n\u2022 Related consults: [Sepsis](#/tree/sepsis/node/sepsis-start), sepsis care; [Febrile neutropenia (Oncological Emergencies)](#/tree/oncological-emergencies/node/onc-fn-recognize), cancer pathway.",
        citation: [40, 57],
        next: "tpe-cytopenia-drug",
