        body: "\n\u2022 Not in the guidelines read: a PJP-specific admission rule, oxygen or ICU criteria, a steroid dose, or the TMP-SMX treatment dose in recipients.\n\u2022 AST IDCOP 2019, pneumonia (ungraded): for outpatient care, close monitoring with repeated clinical evaluation is a prerequisite; if this is not feasible or doubts prevail, inpatient management should be favored. Severity scores are not recommended in recipients (strong, very low). [68]\n\u2022 ISHLT 2023, heart (Class I, C): the transplant centre should educate local clinicians to inform it of added antibiotic, antifungal or antiviral therapy and of pneumonia or any respiratory infection. [66]\n\u2022 Review (emergency medicine, 2018; framing only): discusses admission of transplant patients with serious infection and notes pneumonia scores do not account for transplantation; it sets no rule here. [40]\n\u2022 Related consults: [Pneumonia](#/tree/pneumonia/node/pna-start), pneumonia care; [Sepsis](#/tree/sepsis/node/sepsis-start), sepsis care.\nEditor note: disposition is decided with the treating transplant team.",
        recommendation: "**Possible Pneumocystis pneumonia: PJP-specific admission criteria, oxygen or ICU criteria and treatment doses are not in the guidelines read.** AST IDCOP 2019, pneumonia: for outpatient care, inpatient management is favored if monitoring is not feasible or doubts prevail. Editor note: disposition is decided with the treating transplant team.",
        citation: [66, 68, 40],
