        type: "result",
        module: 3,
        title: "Disposition with possible PTLD",
        safetyLevel: "warning",
        confidence: "consider",
        summary: "Not in the guidelines read: a PTLD admission rule or ED test list. ISHLT 2023, heart (Class I, C): initial PTLD evaluation and plan at the transplant centre.",
        body: "\n\u2022 Not in the guidelines read: when to admit for suspected PTLD, an ED test list, or an imaging rule.\n\u2022 Nearest sourced fact: ISHLT 2023, heart (Class I, C): initial PTLD evaluation and plan should be done at the transplant centre by physicians familiar with transplant-associated malignancies. [73]\n\u2022 Review (Semin Nephrol 2024; framing only): collaboration between specialists is essential when weighing PTLD timing, immunosuppression, graft function and histology. [75]\n\u2022 Review (emergency medicine, 2018; framing only): discusses admission of transplant patients with serious infection; it is not about PTLD and sets no rule here. [40]\n\u2022 Related consults: [Oncological Emergencies](#/tree/oncological-emergencies/node/onc-start), cancer emergencies; [Sepsis](#/tree/sepsis/node/sepsis-start), sepsis care.\nEditor note: disposition is decided with the treating transplant team.",
        recommendation: "**Possible PTLD: an admission rule, ED tests and imaging are not in the guidelines read.** ISHLT 2023, heart (Class I, C): initial PTLD evaluation and plan at the transplant centre. Editor note: disposition is decided with the treating transplant team.",
